    {
        "name": "Ovarian Cysts",
        "name_ja": "卵巣嚢胞",
        "symptoms": {"abdominal_distension", "aggressive_behavior", "hair_loss", "vulvar_swelling"},
        "description": "Ovarian cysts in chinchillas are fluid-filled sacs developing in ovaries, moderately common in intact females >3 years old (20-40% of unspayed chinchillas by age 4-5). Cysts result from persistent follicle stimulation or corpus luteum persistence; estrogen secretion causes prolonged estrus, vulvar swelling, aggression, and alopecia (symmetrical fur loss on flanks/rump). CRITICAL: chinchillas can develop rapid septic complications if cyst ruptures (36-48 hour window to septic shock); thermoregulation must be strictly maintained post-op (15-22°C non-negotiable). Risk of rupture with internal bleeding, secondary neoplasia (5% of cases), or cyst torsion. Diagnosis via ultrasound; surgical treatment (OVE/OVH) is definitive cure.",
        "description_ja": "チンチラの卵巣嚢胞は液体で満たされた嚢胞で、未避妘雌（>3歳）に中程度に多い（避妘なし雌の20-40%が4-5歳までに）。エストロゲン分泌による延長発情・外陰腫脹・攻撃性・脱毛。重大：チンチラは破裂時に急速敗血症進行（36-48時間で敗血症ショック）；術後温度調節が厳格に必須（15-22°C 不可侵）。破裂で内出血、二次肉芽膜細胞腫（5%）、捻転。超音波で確定診断；手術（OVE/OVH）で根治。",
        "urgency": "high",
        "recommended_tests": ["abdominal_ultrasound", "hormone_panel", "physical_exam", "blood_chemistry"],
        "causes": "Persistent gonadotropin stimulation of ovarian follicles (FSH-responsive cysts), persistent corpus luteum formation (luteal cysts), or impaired ovulation. Risk factors: intact status, age >3 years (cumulative estrogen exposure), genetic predisposition, dietary factors (inadequate vitamin E/selenium increases oxidative stress), stress (alters GnRH pulsatility), previous dystocia or reproductive trauma, environmental temperature instability (chinchillas are extremely sensitive to thermal stress).",
        "causes_ja": "持続的ゴナドトロピン刺激（FSH産生嚢胞）、持続黄体形成、排卵障害。危険因子：避妘なし、>3歳年齢、遺伝的素因、栄養（ビタミンE/セレン不足）、ストレス、難産既往、温度不安定性。",
        "pathophysiology": "Ovarian follicles fail to ovulate, accumulating fluid under continued FSH stimulation. Granulosa cells secrete estrogen even without ovulation, causing prolonged estral cycling. Estrogen-induced fur loss occurs symmetrically on flanks/rump. Vulvar swelling (characteristic vulvar edema) occurs from chronic estrogenization. Cyst rupture causes acute hemorrhage into peritoneal cavity—in chinchillas (2.5-3.5 kg body mass), hemorrhage rapidly triggers thermoregulatory dysregulation and septic cascade. Torsion of ovarian pedicle causes acute vascular compromise and ovarian infarction, presenting as acute abdomen with severe pain. Chinchillas' rapid metabolic rate and thermoregulatory sensitivity mean that any peritoneal irritation (from rupture or torsion) rapidly cascades to multi-system failure. Secondary malignant transformation (5% of cases) to granulosa cell tumor or adenocarcinoma occurs with chronic cyst persistence. Chronic estrogen exposure increases endometrial hyperplasia and pyometra risk even in non-breeding animals.",
        "pathophysiology_ja": "卵胞が排卵不全で液体蓄積。顆粒膜細胞がエストロゲン分泌（無排卵でも）で延長発情周期。エストロゲン誘発脱毛が対称性側腹部に。外陰腫脹が慢性エストロゲン化から。嚢胞破裂で腹腔急性出血—チンチラ（2.5-3.5 kg）で出血が急速体温調節障害と敗血症カスケード誘発。卵巣茎捻転で血管圧迫と梗塞。チンチラの急速代謝率と体温調節敏感性は腹膜刺激が多システム不全に急速進行。5%で肉芽膜細胞腫/腺癌に転化。慢性エストロゲン曝露で子宮内膜過形成と子宮蓄膿症リスク。",
        "treatment": "TREATMENT OPTIONS (choose based on cyst characteristics, age, breeding status): 1) MEDICAL MANAGEMENT (trial 4-8 weeks for functional cysts with minimal symptoms): a) GnRH AGONIST: Deslorelin implant 4.7 mg SC (causes desensitization of pituitary, suppresses FSH; lasts 3-6 months). Monitor ultrasound at weeks 4-6 (cyst size should decrease 30-50% if FSH-responsive). b) hCG: 500-1,000 IU/kg IM every 7 days × 2-3 doses (triggers ovulation in functional cysts). Monitor for estrus cessation. c) MONITORING: weekly ultrasound × 4 weeks, then monthly. If cyst persists >4-8 weeks despite medical management → surgical removal indicated. 2) SURGICAL MANAGEMENT (OVE/OVH—DEFINITIVE; recommended for cysts >15 mm, multiple cysts, symptoms refractory to medical management, or cyst rupture): a) PRE-OPERATIVE ASSESSMENT: ultrasound to assess cyst characteristics (simple vs complex/hemorrhagic), size, evidence of rupture, concurrent uterine pathology. Blood chemistry for anesthetic risk. b) ANESTHESIA PROTOCOL (CRITICAL for chinchilla thermoregulation): pre-medication dexmedetomidine 2-5 μg/kg IM (lower dose than guinea pig to avoid excessive bradycardia), mask induction isoflurane (vaporizer 3-4%), maintain 1.5-2.5% isoflurane in oxygen. CRITICAL: use warm IV fluids (37°C) during surgery, ensure surgery time minimal <30 min (chinchillas crash rapidly under anesthesia). Pre-warm surgical drapes. Post-anesthesia, provide external heat source immediately. c) SURGICAL TECHNIQUE: ventral midline laparotomy (15-20 mm incision), exteriorize ovary carefully (avoid cyst rupture—gentle handling critical), ligate ovarian and uterine vessels with 4-0 silk or absorbable suture. Option 1: Partial OVE (remove affected ovary only if unaffected ovary looks normal and breeding possible). Option 2: Full OVE/OVH (recommended for non-breeding animals due to >50% risk of contralateral cyst development within 12-24 months). Close linea alba with 4-0 absorbable suture, skin with tissue adhesive. d) IF CYST RUPTURE ENCOUNTERED: assess for hemorrhage, irrigate peritoneal cavity gently with warm 0.9% saline, remove clots/blood, ensure hemostasis of ovarian vessel. Watch for ongoing hemorrhage post-op (abdominal distension, lethargy >24h = re-operation needed). 3) PERCUTANEOUS NEEDLE ASPIRATION (temporary relief only; recurrence 80%+): ultrasound-guided fine-needle aspiration under brief isoflurane sedation. Appropriate only as temporary bridge to surgery. 4) POST-OPERATIVE CARE (CRITICAL—temperature control is highest priority): a) TEMPERATURE CONTROL—ABSOLUTELY CRITICAL: maintain STRICT 15-22°C environment (chinchillas cannot tolerate >25°C; even brief overheating is fatal post-op). Use external heat source if needed but keep room temperature cool. Monitor core temperature q2h × 24h. Hypothermia risk: if room is <15°C and external heating insufficient, provide incubator. b) ANALGESIA: meloxicam 0.3-0.5 mg/kg PO q24h × 5-7 days (NOT buprenorphine—opioids suppress GI motility). c) ANTIBIOTICS: enrofloxacin 5-10 mg/kg PO q12h × 14-21 days (if rupture encountered, use 14-21 days; covers gram-negatives from peritoneal translocation). d) SC FLUIDS (do NOT use IV in chinchillas if avoidable): LRS 15-25 mL/kg/day SC × 48-72h (if hemorrhage encountered). Monitor hydration status—chinchillas dehydrate rapidly with decreased oral intake. e) GI SUPPORT: timothy hay ad libitum (must maintain cecal motility post-surgery), high-quality pellets, probiotics (FortiFlora pinch daily × 7-10 days). Monitor fecal output—should resume within 12-24h post-op. f) MONITORING: temperature q2h × 24h, q4h × 24-48h, appetite (should eat within 6-12h), fecal output. Pain assessment (should improve by post-op day 2-3). 5) EMERGENCY COMPLICATIONS: Temperature dysregulation (>25°C or <14°C despite intervention): immediate life threat—correct environment first, may indicate septic shock if fever persists. Hemorrhage: may need re-operation if bleeding uncontrolled. Peritonitis (fever >39°C, abdominal pain): aggressive fluids, maximize antibiotics (add metronidazole 20 mg/kg PO q12h × 10-14 days for anaerobes), consider re-operation if refractory.",
        "treatment_ja": "治療選択肢（嚢胞特性、年齢、育種状態で選択）：1) 医学的管理（機能性嚢胞で最小症状；4-8週試行）：a) GnRH アゴニスト：デスロレリンインプラント 4.7 mg SC（下垂体脱感作で FSH 抑制；3-6ヶ月）。4-6週超音波監視。b) hCG：500-1,000 IU/kg IM q7日 × 2-3回。発情停止監視。c) 監視：週1回超音波 × 4週、その後月1回。4-8週で嚢胞遷延 → 手術適応。2) 外科管理（OVE/OVH—根治的；>15 mm嚢胞、複数、医学的難治、破裂時で推奨）：a) 術前評価：超音波嚢胞特性評価、破裂証拠、子宮病理。血液化学。b) 麻酔プロトコル（重大：チンチラ体温調節）：デクスメデトミジン 2-5 μg/kg IM、マスク導入イソフルラン、維持 1.5-2.5%。重大：温 IV 輸液（37°C）、手術時間 <30分。c) 手術：腹部正中小開腸（15-20 mm）、卵巣を優しく外側化、血管結紮。選択肢1：部分OVE。選択肢2：全OVE/OVH（推奨）。d) 破裂時：灌流、止血確認。3) 経皮針吸引（一時的；再発80%+）。4) 術後管理（重大—温度制御が最優先）：a) 温度管理—絶対重大：厳格 15-22°C 環境（>25°C 不耐容；術後加熱が致命的）。q2h 温度監視。b) 鎮痛：メロキシカム 0.3-0.5 mg/kg PO q24h × 5-7日。c) 抗菌薬：エンロフロキサシン 5-10 mg/kg PO q12h × 14-21日。d) SC 輸液：LRS 15-25 mL/kg/日 × 48-72h。e) GI 支持：ティモシーヘイ給与量制限なし、プロバイオティクス。f) 監視：q2h 温度 × 24h、食欲、排便。5) 緊急合併症：温度調節不全（>25°C または <14°C）：直ちに生命脅威。出血：再手術。腹膜炎：積極的輸液、抗菌薬最大化。",
        "prevention": "CRITICAL PREVENTION: 1) SPAYING—MOST EFFECTIVE: Ovariohysterectomy before age 3 years (prevents essentially all cyst development if done before cyst formation). Recommend OVE/OVH in all non-breeding females by 24-30 months of age. Early spaying also prevents secondary uterine disease (hyperplasia, pyometra—30-50% incidence in unspayed chinchillas by age 5-6). 2) BREEDING MANAGEMENT (for breeding females): Select for genetic resistance (avoid females with cyst history or whose mothers had cysts). Breed females ONLY between 18-48 months of age (avoid <18 months—immature; avoid >48 months—cyst risk 60%+). Retire breeding females by age 4 years and spay. Mandatory yearly ultrasound screening starting age 2 years (detect cysts early). 3) NUTRITION (supportive): Vitamin E 20-50 IU/kg/day (antioxidant support—chinchillas don't synthesize vitamin E), selenium 0.3-0.5 μg/kg/day (cofactor for antioxidant enzymes), adequate vitamin A, calcium 0.8-1.2% diet. High-quality timothy hay unlimited, balanced pellets 10-15g/day, limited treats (avoid high-fat treats that increase estrogenic activity). 4) TEMPERATURE MANAGEMENT: maintain STRICT 15-22°C environment (ABSOLUTELY CRITICAL for chinchilla health—temperature fluctuation increases stress hormones and GnRH pulsatility abnormalities, predisposing to cysts). Avoid >25°C (fatal heat stress risk), avoid <12°C (hypothermia stress). Consistent 12h light/dark cycle. 5) STRESS REDUCTION: minimize handling of intact females, avoid cage mate conflict, maintain quiet environment (loud noise increases cortisol and suppresses reproductive hormone regulation). 6) MONITORING (breeding females retained): yearly ultrasound starting age 2 years (assess ovarian volume, cyst presence/size). If ultrasound shows cyst >10 mm, discuss management (medical vs surgical). If multiple cysts or rapid growth (>3 mm/month), recommend OVE. 7) POST-DYSTOCIA CARE: females with dystocia history have increased secondary cyst formation due to endometrial inflammation—recommend OVE post-recovery rather than re-breeding.",
        "prevention_ja": "重大予防：1) 避妘—最も効果的：OVE/OVH を3歳前（嚢胞発生前で本質的に全予防）。24-30ヶ月齢までに全非育種雌に推奨。早期避妘で子宮疾患（5-6歳で30-50%）も予防。2) 育種管理（育種雌）：遺伝的抵抗性選別。18-48ヶ月齢のみ育種（<18ヶ月回避；>48ヶ月回避—嚢胞リスク60%+）。4歳で退役・避妘。2歳から年1回超音波。3) 栄養：ビタミンE 20-50 IU/kg/日（チンチラはE合成不可）、セレン 0.3-0.5 μg/kg/日、ビタミンA、カルシウム 0.8-1.2%。4) 温度管理：厳格 15-22°C 維持（重大—温度変動はストレスホルモンと GnRH 異常増加）。>25°C 回避（致死的熱ストレス）、<12°C 回避。12h 明暗周期。5) ストレス軽減：避妘なし雌取扱い最小化、ケージメイト紛争回避、静環境。6) 監視（育種雌）：2歳から年1回超音波。>10 mm 嚢胞 → 管理相談。複数嚢胞または急速成長 → OVE推奨。7) 難産後ケア：OVE推奨。",
        "prognosis": "EXCELLENT with early surgical intervention in younger chinchillas: With OVE/OVH in chinchillas <4 years old, cure rate >95%, normal remaining lifespan achievable (chinchillas can live 5-8 years total; early intervention preserves quality of life for remaining years). Medical management success (GnRH agonist trial) 50-70% for FSH-responsive functional cysts; however, >60% recur within 6-12 months if ovaries retained. Without treatment: simple cysts may persist asymptomatically for 1-2 years (no treatment needed if <15 mm and non-symptomatic), but 5-10% rupture spontaneously causing acute hemorrhage (mortality 30-50% even with emergency treatment due to rapid septic cascade in chinchillas). Functional cysts show variable course—some regress spontaneously (15-25%), others progress to large, hormone-secreting cysts requiring surgery. Long-term: unspayed females with cysts have >50% risk of developing concurrent uterine disease (pyometra, hyperplasia) within 12-24 months even if ovarian cysts managed medically. Secondary malignant transformation: 5% of persistent cysts >12 months develop adenocarcinoma/granulosa cell tumor (mortality near 100% if diagnosed—metastatic spread common). Post-surgical prognosis: chinchillas surviving OVE/OVH have excellent remaining lifespan; quality of life dramatically improves (fur regrowth 4-6 weeks, behavioral normalization 1-2 weeks).",
        "prognosis_ja": "若いチンチラでの早期手術介入で優秀：OVE/OVH を <4歳で実施で治癒率 >95%、正常残存寿命達成。医学的管理成功（GnRH アゴニスト試行）FSH反応性嚢胞で 50-70%；但し卵巣保持で >60% が 6-12ヶ月以内に再発。無治療で単純嚢胞は無症状で1-2年遷延（<15 mm で治療不要），但し 5-10% が自発破裂（急性出血で死亡率 30-50%—チンチラで敗血症カスケード急速）。機能性嚢胞は可変進過—15-25% が自然消退、他は大型ホルモン分泌嚢胞で手術要。長期：未避妘嚢胞雌で >50% が 12-24ヶ月で並存子宮疾患（子宮蓄膿症、過形成）発生。悪性転化：5% で死亡率 ~100%。術後生活の質が劇的改善（毛皮再生 4-6週、行動正常化 1-2週）。",
        "onset_pattern": {"subacute", "chronic"},
        "age_predisposition": {"adult", "senior"},
    },
    {
        "name": "Endometritis",
        "name_ja": "子宮内膜炎",
        "symptoms": {"appetite_loss", "fever", "lethargy", "vaginal_discharge"},
        "description": "Endometritis is acute inflammation and bacterial infection of the uterine endometrium, often postpartum or secondary to hormonal imbalances. Can progress to pyometra within 48-72 hours if untreated. Chinchillas show rapid clinical deterioration due to small body size.",
        "description_ja": "子宮内膜の炎症と感染で、子宮蓄膿症に進行する可能性があります。チンチラは小体格のため急速に悪化。",
        "urgency": "high",
        "recommended_tests": [
            "abdominal_ultrasound",
            "vaginal_cytology",
            "blood_chemistry",
            "culture_sensitivity",
            "complete_blood_count",
        ],
        "causes": "Bacterial colonization of the uterine endometrium, often postpartum (retained placenta, birthing trauma) or secondary to hormonal imbalances (prolonged estrus cycle, ovarian cysts, estrogen toxicity). Common bacteria: Staphylococcus aureus, E. coli, Pasteurella multocida, Streptococcus spp. Risk factors: multiparous females (>3-4 litters), dystocia history, poor hygiene, stress, immune suppression, inadequate calcium/vitamin C intake.",
        "causes_ja": "チンチラにおける子宮内膜炎の原因：産後細菌コロニー化（胎盤貯留、産傷）またはホルモン不均衡に二次的（延長発情周期、卵巣嚢胞、エストロゲン毒性）。黄色ブドウ球菌、E. coli、多様性パスツレラ、連鎖球菌が最多。危険因子：多産雌（>3-4産仔）、難産既往、不衛生、ストレス、免疫抑制、不足カルシウム/ビタミンC。",
        "pathophysiology": "Endometritis develops when bacteria colonize the endometrium, triggering acute inflammatory cascade: bacterial endotoxins → neutrophil infiltration → cytokine release (TNF-α, IL-6) → tissue edema/congestion. Myometrial contractions attempt clearance but are impaired by endotoxemia. In chinchillas (small body mass 2.5-3.5 kg), endotoxemia rapidly causes systemic effects: fever→tachycardia (HR >300 bpm)→hypotension→shock potential. If untreated >48-72 hours, endometritis progresses to closed-type pyometra (no drainage), leading to explosive sepsis. Estrogen toxicity (in prolonged estrus) worsens endometrial damage and impairs immune response.",
        "pathophysiology_ja": "子宮内膜炎はチンチラにおける生殖器疾患で、細菌が子宮内膜にコロニー化して急性炎症カスケード発動。細菌エンドトキシン→好中球浸潤→サイトカイン放出（TNF-α、IL-6）→組織浮腫/充血。筋層収縮が排液を試みるがエンドトキシム血症で障害。チンチラでは小体格（2.5-3.5 kg）でエンドトキシム血症が急速に全身効果を起こす：発熱→頻脈（HR>300 bpm）→低血圧→ショック可能。無治療で>48-72時間、子宮内膜炎が閉鎖型子宮蓄膿症（排液なし）に進行→爆発的敗血症。エストロゲン毒性（延長発情）が子宮内膜損傷を悪化させ免疫応答を障害。",
        "treatment": "EARLY MEDICAL MANAGEMENT (optimal if caught within 24-48 hours before pyometra develops): IV crystalloid fluids (LRS 50-100 mL/kg bolus to restore perfusion), analgesia (meloxicam 0.2-0.3 mg/kg SC q24h × 5-7 days), broad-spectrum antibiotics (NO β-LACTAMS—fatal dysbiosis in chinchillas): Enrofloxacin 10-15 mg/kg PO/SC q12h × 14-21 days (first-line; excellent uterine penetration) OR trimethoprim-sulfamethoxazole (TMS) 30 mg/kg PO q12h × 14-21 days as alternative. Add metronidazole 20 mg/kg PO q12h × 10-14 days (covers anaerobes, prevents polymicrobial infection). Vitamin C 50-100 mg/kg/day SC/PO (chinchillas synthesize C but stress depletes—immune support critical). Hepatic support: silymarin 20-40 mg/kg/day PO × 14 days (endotoxemia causes liver dysfunction). Culture sensitivity testing essential—switch to organism-directed antibiotic once culture results available. Uterine drainage: if ultrasound shows significant fluid accumulation (>5 mm), consider transcervical flush (0.9% saline 10-20 mL via small catheter) under sedation to remove purulent material (NOT routine, only if significant accumulation). CRITICAL MONITORING: daily temperature assessment (fever persistence >3-5 days = treatment failure), vaginal discharge character (should resolve within 3-5 days), blood work at days 7 and 14 (WBC normalization, resolution of left shift). If fever persists >5 days or discharge worsens: assume progression to pyometra or treatment failure→EMERGENCY SURGICAL OVE. SURGICAL MANAGEMENT (if medical management fails or closed-type pyometra suspected): Emergency OVE under isoflurane anesthesia (see Pyometra entry for non-narcotic anesthesia protocol and surgical technique). Post-operative: continue IV fluids, antibiotics, analgesia as above × 10-14 days post-op. Prognosis is better if caught as endometritis (medical success 60-80%); worse if progressed to pyometra.",
        "treatment_ja": "早期医学的管理（最適—子宮蓄膿症発展前24-48時間で捕捉時）：IV結晶質輸液（乳酸リンガー50-100 mL/kg bolus灌流復旧）、鎮痛（メロキシカム0.2-0.3 mg/kg SC q24h × 5-7日）、広域抗菌薬（βラクタム禁止—チンチラで致死的dysbiosis）：エンロフロキサシン10-15 mg/kg PO/SC q12h × 14-21日（第一選択；優れた子宮浸透）OR TMS 30 mg/kg PO q12h × 14-21日。メトロニダゾール20 mg/kg PO q12h × 10-14日を追加（嫌気性菌カバー）。ビタミンC 50-100 mg/kg/日 SC/PO。肝臓支持：シリマリン20-40 mg/kg/日 PO × 14日。培養感受性試験必須—培養結果で生物体指向抗菌薬に変更。子宮排液：超音波で著しい液体蓄積（>5 mm）を示す場合、経頸部洗浄（0.9%生食10-20 mL小カテーテル経由）を鎮静下で考慮（常規ではなく著しい蓄積の場合）。重大監視：毎日体温評価（発熱遷延>3-5日=治療失敗）、膣分泌物文字（3-5日内に解決すべき）、血液検査（7日と14日で好中球正常化、左方移動解決）。発熱遷延>5日または分泌物悪化：子宮蓄膿症進行または治療失敗と仮定→緊急外科OVE。外科管理（医学的管理失敗または閉鎖型子宮蓄膿症疑い時）：イソフルラン麻酔下緊急OVE（子宮蓄膿症エントリで非麻薬性麻酔プロトコルと外科手術を参照）。術後：IV輸液、抗菌薬、鎮痛を上記通り × 術後10-14日継続。予後は子宮内膜炎として捕捉した場合が良好（医学的成功60-80%）；子宮蓄膿症に進行した場合は不良。",
        "prevention": "CRITICAL PREVENTION: 1) Spay all females not intended for breeding by 12 months age (prevents estrogen-induced endometrial damage). 2) Maintain strict hygiene: clean bedding daily (aspen/paper-based, NOT cedar/pine), spot-clean soiled areas, disinfect cage biweekly. 3) Optimize nutrition: vitamin C 50-100 mg/kg/day (immune support; stress depletes), calcium 1,000-1,500 mg/kg diet, quality timothy hay unlimited (>70%). 4) Stress reduction: minimize handling of intact females, maintain cool temperature (15-22°C), avoid overcrowding. 5) Monitor breeding females: monthly abdominal palpation (detect uterine enlargement early), quarterly ultrasound if >18 months old (detect early endometrial changes before endometritis develops). 6) Avoid prolonged estrus cycles: monitor cycling females—if straining/genital swelling persists >3-4 days, may indicate ovarian cyst or hormonal dysfunction (ultrasound evaluation needed). 7) Prompt postpartum care: ensure complete placental passage, monitor for vaginal discharge (clear mucus normal <2 days; purulent discharge = emergency). 8) Spay post-recovery if endometritis occurs (60-80% recurrence risk if attempt rebreeding without OVE).",
        "prevention_ja": "重大予防：1) 12ヶ月齢までに育種意図なし全雌を避妊（エストロゲン誘導子宮内膜損傷予防）。2) 厳密衛生管理：毎日清潔床材（アスペン/紙ベース、スギ/マツ禁止）、汚れた部位spot-clean、隔週ケージ消毒。3) 栄養最適化：ビタミンC 50-100 mg/kg/日（免疫支持；ストレスで枯渇）、カルシウム1,000-1,500 mg/kg食、品質チモシーヘイ無制限。4) ストレス低減：避妊されない雌取扱い最小化、冷温維持（15-22°C）、過密防止。5) 育種雌監視：月1回腹部触診（子宮腫大早期検出）、>18ヶ月齢なら四半期超音波（子宮内膜炎前の早期変化検出）。6) 延長発情周期回避：周期雌監視—緊張/外陰腫脹が>3-4日遷延する場合、卵巣嚢胞またはホルモン機能障害の可能性（超音波評価必要）。7) 迅速産後管理：完全胎盤脱出確保、膣分泌物モニタリング（透明粘液は正常<2日；化膿性分泌物=緊急）。8) 回復後避妘（子宮内膜炎発生時再発リスク60-80% OVEなしで再繁殖試みたら）。",
        "prognosis": "GUARDED to GOOD if medical management initiated within 24-48 hours: success rate 60-80% with appropriate antibiotics and supportive care. Fever resolution within 3-7 days is good prognostic sign. If endometritis persists >5-7 days despite treatment or converts to pyometra: prognosis becomes POOR (see Pyometra entry—mortality 85-98% without OVE). CRITICAL: Chinchillas are small (2.5-3.5 kg) and deteriorate rapidly; delay in diagnosis/treatment rapidly worsens prognosis. Recurrence risk if survived without OVE: 60-80% (virtually all survivors develop pyometra or repeat endometritis within 6-12 months). Mandatory OVE post-recovery (cannot retry breeding—endometrial damage is permanent; risk of life-threatening pyometra in future pregnancy unacceptable). Fertility is permanently lost after endometritis (even if uterus retained, endometrial scarring prevents implantation).",
        "prognosis_ja": "子宮内膜炎の予後：慎重〜良好—医学的管理を24-48時間以内に開始した場合：成功率60-80%（適切な抗菌薬と支持療法）。3-7日以内に発熱解決は良好予後徴候。子宮内膜炎が>5-7日遷延または子宮蓄膿症に転換の場合：予後は不良（子宮蓄膿症エントリ参照—OVEなし死亡率85-98%）。重大：チンチラは小型（2.5-3.5 kg）で急速悪化；診断/治療遅延で急速に予後悪化。OVE無しで生存時再発リスク：60-80%。回復後避妘必須。受胎率永久喪失。",
        "onset_pattern": {"acute", "subacute"},
        "age_predisposition": {"adult", "young", "senior"},
    },
