    {
        "name": "Vertebral Disc Disease",
        "name_ja": "椎間板疾患",
        "symptoms": {"back_pain", "hind_limb_weakness", "reluctance_to_move", "urinary_incontinence"},
        "description": "Vertebral Disc Disease is a clinical condition requiring veterinary evaluation, diagnosis, and appropriate treatment.",
        "description_ja": "椎間板の変性またはヘルニアによる脊髄圧迫と神経学的徴候です。",
        "urgency": "high",
        "recommended_tests": ["spinal_xray", "neurological_exam", "mri"],
        "causes": "Degeneration or herniation of intervertebral discs causing spinal cord compression and neurological deficits.",
        "causes_ja": "チンチラにおける椎間板疾患の原因: 椎間板の変性またはヘルニアによる脊髄圧迫と神経学的徴候です。",
        "pathophysiology": "The pathological process involves tissue injury, inflammatory response, and progressive functional impairment. Without intervention, compensatory mechanisms may be overwhelmed, leading to clinical deterioration.",
        "pathophysiology_ja": "椎間板疾患はチンチラにおける神経疾患である。炎症、変性、圧迫、または血管障害による中枢・末梢神経系の損傷を伴う。解剖学的位置に応じて運動機能、感覚処理、自律神経調節、認知状態に影響を及ぼす。脱髄、軸索変性、ニューロン喪失は不可逆的な場合がある。浮腫や腫瘤性病変による頭蓋内圧亢進は脳幹ヘルニアを引き起こしうる。",
        "treatment": "Conservative medical management for mild-moderate cases: strict cage rest in small, single-level enclosure (remove shelves, wheels) for 4-6 weeks minimum. Pain management: meloxicam 0.3-0.5 mg/kg PO/SC q24h (long-term use acceptable with renal monitoring), buprenorphine 0.03-0.05 mg/kg SC q8-12h for acute severe pain, gabapentin 5-10 mg/kg PO q8-12h for neuropathic pain. Muscle relaxant: diazepam 0.5-1 mg/kg PO q12h for acute muscle spasm. Corticosteroids for acute disc herniation with edema: dexamethasone 0.2-0.5 mg/kg IV/IM once (NOT with concurrent NSAIDs). Supportive care: padded substrate (fleece), assisted feeding if unable to reach food, bladder expression q6-8h if urinary incontinence present, physiotherapy during recovery. Surgical decompression (hemilaminectomy) for severe/progressive neurological deficits — requires specialist and advanced imaging (CT/MRI). Post-operative antibiotics: enrofloxacin 5-15 mg/kg SC q12h (NEVER oral beta-lactams). Environmental temperature 15-21°C. Prevent falls: low-level housing only during recovery. Monitor deep pain perception — loss of deep pain carries poor prognosis.",
        "treatment_ja": "軽度〜中等度の保存的内科管理: 低い単層ケージでの厳格なケージレスト（棚、ホイールの撤去）最低4-6週間。疼痛管理: メロキシカム 0.3-0.5mg/kg PO/SC q24h（腎モニタリングしつつ長期使用可）、急性重度疼痛にブプレノルフィン 0.03-0.05mg/kg SC q8-12h、神経因性疼痛にガバペンチン 5-10mg/kg PO q8-12h。筋弛緩薬: 急性筋攣縮にジアゼパム 0.5-1mg/kg PO q12h。浮腫を伴う急性椎間板ヘルニアにステロイド: デキサメタゾン 0.2-0.5mg/kg IV/IM単回投与（NSAIDsとの併用禁忌）。支持療法: パッド付き基材（フリース）、食事に届けない場合の給餌補助、尿失禁時のq6-8h膀胱圧迫排尿、回復期の理学療法。重度/進行性神経障害には外科的除圧術（片側椎弓切除術）— 専門医と高度画像（CT/MRI）が必要。術後抗菌薬: エンロフロキサシン 5-15mg/kg SC q12h（経口βラクタム系は絶対禁忌）。環境温度15-21℃。回復期は落下防止のため低い住環境のみ。深部痛覚のモニタリング — 深部痛覚消失は予後不良。",
        "prevention": "Prevention includes appropriate husbandry, balanced nutrition, regular veterinary examinations, stress reduction, and prompt treatment of early signs of illness.",
        "prevention_ja": "椎間板疾患の予防: 適切な運動と体重管理。安全な飼育環境（落下防止、滑り止め）。カルシウム・ビタミンDの適切な摂取。高所からのジャンプを制限。",
        "prognosis": "Prognosis depends on disease severity, timeliness of intervention, and response to treatment. Early diagnosis and appropriate therapy generally improve outcomes.",
        "prognosis_ja": "椎間板疾患の予後: 骨折は適切な固定で予後良好。変性性疾患は進行性だが疼痛管理でQOL維持可能。若齢動物は回復力が高い。",
        "onset_pattern": {"acute", "subacute"},
        "age_predisposition": {"adult", "young", "senior"},
    },
